From e81f138990c2f76531cf4dda24a62df7f0bebe0e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 01:07:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/57] fix-sec-3: S-4 residual: Amazon links on-host, beta
 links only on their company's hosts, no dead Apply button

- server/sources/amazon.js#amazonPostingUrl: the API's job_path is kept verbatim only when the joined
  URL is https on www.amazon.jobs with no userinfo; else /en/jobs/<id>.
- server/normalize.js#postingUrl(u, company): a beta built-in's link must be https, with no userinfo or
  port, on its own registry entry's postingHosts / postingPrefixes (server/companies.js#postingRule).
  Real links of every beta board are unchanged (fixtures; 37,619 links in today's crawl).
- scripts/links-policy.js builds BETA_POSTING_HOSTS / _PREFIXES from those entries (same lists); the
  stable site's lib/companies.js drops beta entries, so no beta host ships there.
- public/app.js: a posting with no http(s) link has no Apply button; the drawer foot says
  "No link to the posting".
Tests: S-4 residual un-todo'd; test/fix-sec-3.test.js; test/e2e/fix-sec-3.e2e.js (registered).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014jaqot5Ddmi7Co6CofBiyc
(cherry picked from commit fe41715a9ae0adf66f5d0a6cf125e19fed614ba7)
